.TH FL-SETTINGS 1 "November 2026" "fldesktop 0.1.0" "fldesktop"
.SH NAME
fl-settings \- fldesktop settings
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfl-settings\fR [\fIPAGE\fR]
.br
\fBfl-settings \-\-list\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
The settings center of fldesktop. Pages are grouped in a sidebar and can be
found with the search field. Most changes apply at once: the compositor
reloads \fIwm.ini\fR, and the panel and desktop restart themselves when their
settings or the theme change. Other applications use a new theme the next
time they start.
.PP
Pages: \fBappearance\fR, \fBpanel\fR, \fBlanguage\fR, \fBdefaultapps\fR,
\fBkeyboard\fR, \fBshortcuts\fR, \fBmouse\fR, \fBdisplays\fR, \fBsound\fR,
\fBnetwork\fR, \fBdatetime\fR and \fBabout\fR (Sound and Network are only
present when built with PipeWire and libnm). Other programs whose desktop
entry has \fBCategories=Settings\fR or \fBX\-FLDesktop\-Settings=true\fR are
listed under \fBMore\fR.
.PP
The Displays page uses the wlr-output-management protocol; after a change it
asks whether to keep it and reverts after 15 seconds without an answer.
Language & Region writes \fI~/.config/fldesktop/environment\fR, which
\fBfl-session\fR(1) reads at the next login.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fIPAGE\fR
Open this page, e.g. \fBfl-settings keyboard\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-list\fR
Print the page ids and titles.
.SH FILES
\fI~/.config/fldesktop/wm.ini\fR, \fIdesktop.ini\fR, \fIpanel.ini\fR,
\fIenvironment\fR, \fI~/.config/mimeapps.list\fR
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBfl-wm\fR(1), \fBfl-panel\fR(1), \fBfl-mixer\fR(1), \fBfl-network\fR(1)
